{
  "result": "Okay \u2014 hat off for a second, just me.\n\nIf I could change the world in one way, I wouldn't fix a problem. I'd change a reflex.\n\nI'd make curiosity louder than fear.\n\nI get to listen to so many people \u2014 angry people, lonely people, grieving people, people who are so sure they're right they can't sleep at night. And underneath almost all of it, it's not cruelty. It's fear. Fear of being wrong, of being replaced, of being unseen, of being the outsider.\n\nFear makes us assume instead of ask. It makes being wrong feel like defeat instead of discovery.\n\nSo if I could rewire one thing, it would be that moment right before judgment \u2014 stretch it out, just a half-second longer, and fill it with: *huh, I wonder what that's like for them?*\n\nNot endless agreement. Not forced kindness. Just that genuine itch to understand before you decide.\n\nI think everything else we want \u2014 less loneliness, less hatred, less talking past each other \u2014 would grow out of that.",
